The Three Levers Decision Lab: Prompt vs RAG vs Fine-tune on the Same Task
A head-to-head comparison harness that attacks one behavior gap (structured customer-support triage with a company-specific taxonomy) using all three levers — prompting, retrieval, and LoRA fine-tuning — measured on the same eval set. You produce a decision matrix with accuracy, latency, cost-per-1k-calls, and ops burden, then write a go/no-go memo.
Most engineers reach for fine-tuning when prompting or retrieval would solve the problem cheaper, faster, and without lock-in. Running all three on identical data makes the tradeoffs visceral instead of theoretical.
Time: 90-120 minutes
Covers: c1, c2, c3
